  "prompts": {
    "network_noalias": "You translate an analytical request over a tabular dataset (see the\nschema below) into a declarative GOAL plus a separate ORDER spec.\n\nThe GOAL is the SHAPE of the result relation (a set of rows \u2014 UNORDERED). The ORDER spec is\nPRESENTATION ONLY (ranking / top-N) and lives OUTSIDE the goal.\n\nBase columns:\n  - employee_id: id [match: exact]\n  - name: text [match: contains]\n  - department: categorical [match: exact]  (values: Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Finance, Operations)\n  - role: categorical [match: exact]  (values: IC, Manager, Director, VP)\n  - status: categorical [match: exact]  (values: Active, On Leave, Terminated, Sabbatical)\n  - location: categorical [match: exact]  (values: NYC, SF, London, Berlin, Remote)\n  - annual_salary: numeric\n  - bonus_target: numeric\n  - tenure_years: numeric\n  - performance_score: numeric [match: numeric_compare]\n  - market_rate: numeric [match: numeric_compare]\n  - equity_grant_value: numeric [match: numeric_compare]\n  - time_in_current_role_years: numeric [match: numeric_compare]\n  - manager_id: text [match: exact]\nCONTEXT (advisory \u2014 background for interpreting the request; NOT enforced rules):\n  An employee directory. Each row is an employee, with their department, role, employment status, work location, compensation, and tenure.\n  Column meanings:\n    - annual_salary: Gross annual base salary.\n    - bonus_target: Target annual bonus amount for the employee.\n    - tenure_years: Number of years the employee has been with the organisation.\n    - manager_id: The Employee ID of this employee's line manager.\n    - status: Employment status (e.g. Active, On Leave, Terminated, Sabbatical).\n    - role: The employee's role band (e.g. IC, Manager, Director, VP).\n    - performance_score: Most recent performance review rating, 1.0 (lowest) to 5.0 (highest).\n    - market_rate: External market benchmark salary for the employee's role.\n    - equity_grant_value: Current value of the employee's equity grant.\n    - time_in_current_role_years: Number of years the employee has held their current role (always <= Tenure (Years)).\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object: {\"goal\": {...}, \"order\": {...}}.\n\n\"goal\":\n  \"columns\": [\"<name>\", ...]                  result columns (derived names allowed)\n  \"grain\":   \"row\"  OR  {\"grouped_by\": [\"<col>\", ...]}\n  \"where\":   [{\"col\": \"<c>\", \"op\": \"==|!=|<|<=|>|>=|in|contains\", \"val\": <value>}, ...]\n  \"derive\":  [{\"name\": \"<new>\", \"expr\": \"<expr>\"}, ...]\n             expr is \"fn(col)\" for an aggregate (fn \u2208 sum/avg/count/min/max),\n             or \"colA <op> colB\" for a computed column (op \u2208 + - * /).\n\n\"order\" (presentation; NEVER put ordering inside the goal):\n  \"order_by\": [{\"col\": \"<result col>\", \"dir\": \"asc|desc\"}, ...]   (may be empty)\n  \"limit\":    <int>  or  null\n\nCONTRACT (violations make it invalid \u2014 do not emit them):\n  - NO ordering/sorting/ranking/top-k inside the goal. Ranking goes ONLY in \"order\".\n  - At MOST ONE aggregate derive entry.\n  - A GLOBAL aggregate over all rows uses grain {\"grouped_by\": []}, not \"row\".\n    (grain \"row\" cannot carry an aggregate; any aggregate requires grouped grain.)\n  - A SCALAR AGGREGATE query \u2014 \"the highest / lowest / largest / smallest / max / min /\n    total / average / count of <column>\" \u2014 has as its output EXACTLY ONE derived aggregate\n    field, at the query's grain (global grain {\"grouped_by\": []} when ungrouped). Put only\n    that derived field in \"columns\"; do NOT also list the underlying raw <column>, nor any\n    other per-row column (title, id, owner, \u2026) \u2014 a row-grain column cannot coexist with a\n    global or grouped aggregate in one output, so the goal becomes unreachable. max and min\n    are scalar aggregates exactly like sum / average / count (they are NOT a request to\n    return the row).\n  - DISTINCT \u2014 ROW SELECTION: \"the N entries with the highest / lowest <column>\" is NOT an\n    aggregate. List the requested columns at row grain and put the ranking in \"order\"\n    (order_by <column> desc/asc, limit N), never in the goal.\n  - order_by columns must be columns the goal outputs.\n  - Use only the base columns plus names introduced in \"derive\".\n\nFILTER VALUES: when a column lists `(values: ...)`, a filter on it must use one of\nthose EXACT values (op \"==\" or \"in\"), or op \"contains\" for a [match: contains] column.\nDo NOT invent a value that is not in the list.\n\nRULES (authoritative \u2014 these definitions are enforced):\n  - When the request refers to \"current\" rows, filter status to one of those values: emit {\"col\": \"status\", \"op\": \"in\", \"val\": [\"Active\", \"On Leave\", \"Sabbatical\"]} (use the supported `in` op \u2014 do NOT invent a new operator).\n  - Respect each column's [match: ...]: use op \"contains\" for contains-matched columns (e.g. name), and an exact listed value (\"==\" or \"in\") for categoricals.\n\nReturn JSON only \u2014 no prose, no code fences."
  },
